368</fpage><lpage>2372</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6327396</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Coxetal1997"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cox</surname><given-names>D.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cui</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Aldrich</surname><given-names>R.W.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Allosteric gating of a large conductance Ca-activated K<sup>+</sup> channel</article-title><source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source><volume>110</volume><year>1997</year><fpage>257</fpage><lpage>281</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9276753</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CoxandAldrich2000"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cox</surname><given-names>D.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Aldrich</surname><given-names>R.W.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Is the BK<sub>Ca</sub> channel's Ca<sup>2+</sup> binding affinity enhanced by its &#x003b2;<sub>1</sub> subunit? A simple experiment</article-title><source>Biophys. J.</source><volume>78</volume><year>2000</year><fpage>91A</fpage>(Abstr.)</citation></ref><ref id="Cuietal1997"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cui</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cox</surname><given-names>D.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Aldrich</surname><given-names>R.W.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intrinsic voltage dependence and Ca<sup>2+</sup> regulation of m<italic>slo</italic> large conductance Ca-activated K<sup>+</sup> channels</article-title><source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source><volume>109</volume><year>1997</year><fpage>647</fpage><lpage>673</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9154910</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Diazetal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Diaz</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Meera</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Amigo</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Stefani</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Alvarez</surname><given-names>O.</given-names></name><name><surname>Toro</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Latorre</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of the S4 segment in a voltage-dependent calcium-sensitive potassium (hSlo) channel</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem</source><volume>273</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>32430</fpage><lpage>32436</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9829973</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="DiChiaraandReinhart1995"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>DiChiara</surname><given-names>T.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Reinhart</surname><given-names>P.H.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distinct effects of Ca<sup>2+</sup> and voltage on the activation and deactivation of cloned Ca<sup>2+</sup>-activated K<sup>+</sup> channels</article-title><source>J. Physiol.</source><volume>489</volume><year>1995</year><fpage>403</fpage><lpage>418</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8847636</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Dworetzkyetal1996"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dworetzky</surname><given-names>S.I.</given-names></name><name><surname>Boissard</surname><given-names>C.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lum-Ragan</surname><given-names>J.T.</given-names></name><name><surname>McKay</surname><given-names>M.C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Post-Munson</surname><given-names>D.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Trojnacki</surname><given-names>J.T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>C.P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gribkoff</surname><given-names>V.K.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Phenotypic alteration of a human BK (h<italic>Slo</italic>) channel by h<italic>Slo</italic>&#x003b2; subunit coexpressionchanges in blocker sensitivity, activation/relaxation and inactivation kinetics, and protein kinase A modulation</article-title><source>J. Neurosci.</source><volume>16</volume><year>1996</year><fpage>4543</fpage><lpage>4550</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8764643</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Dworetzkyetal1994"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dworetzky</surname><given-names>S.I.</given-names></name><name><surname>Trojnacki</surname><given-names>J.T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gribkoff</surname><given-names>V.K.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cloning and expression of a human large-conductance calcium-activated potassium channel</article-title><source>Brain Res. Mol. Brain Res</source><volume>27</volume><year>1994</year><fpage>189</fpage><lpage>193</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7877450</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Hamilletal1981"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hamill</surname><given-names>O.P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Marty</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Neher</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakmann</surname><given-names>B.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sigworth</surname><given-names>F.J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Improved patch-clamp techniques for high-resolution current recording from cells and cell-free membrane patches</article-title><source>Pfl&#x000fc;gers Arch.</source><volume>391</volume><year>1981</year><fpage>85</fpage><lpage>100</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="Hille1991"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hille</surname><given-names>B.</given-names></name></person-group><source>Ionic channels of excitable membranes</source>